            {
              "id": "cc225cbe-5152-4154-b698-c078820e0ec7",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Game Makers: The Story of Parker Brothers, from Tiddledy Winks to Trivial Pursuit</strong></em> was written by Philip E. Orbanes, published by Harvard Business Review Press, November 14, 2003."
            },
            {
              "id": "c5cb01d9-0736-4dea-b87d-47417074fcad",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "2bde85f8-69b9-4d6e-ab20-ba00876208fb",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "The Monopoly game, Trivial Pursuit, Clue, Boggle<em>, and </em>Risk<em> are more than games - they're part of Americana. This work presents a study of successful business expansion. It also gives an account of how one individual's strength of character - or weakness - exerted a significant influence over a company's fortunes.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "935fb9f6-8a3e-44ed-959a-c2bc5e0e95bb",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
